 or\, with a particular passion for collaborative playing. She earned a Ba
 chelor of Music\, Master of Music\, and Performer Diploma in Piano Perfor
 mance from Indiana University. She later became the inaugural recipient o
 f the Doctor of Musical Arts in Collaborative Piano degree from the Unive
 rsity of Texas at Austin\, where she studied with Anne Epperson\, current
  chair of Jacobs' Department of Chamber and Collaborative Music.</p>
