 t Major\, Op. 3 (1796)<br /></em>W. A. Mozart: <em>String Quintet in C Ma
 jor\, K.515<br /></em><br /><strong>About the Artists</strong><br /><br /
 >  Israeli-born violist and composer <strong>Atar Arad</strong> is distin
 guished professor of music in viola at the IU Jacobs School of Music. Sum
 mer activities include teaching at Keshet Eilon\, Domaine Forget\, Heifet
 z Institute\, and\, the Steans Music Institute. Cum laude first-prize win
 ner at the Geneva International Music Competition (1972)\, he has perform
 ed worldwide in recitals and as a soloist with major orchestras and was a
  member of the celebrated Cleveland Quartet. Recordings with the quartet 
 and as a soloist for such labels as Teldec\, Telarc\, RCA\, and RIAX are 
